From: Matthew Feickert <matthew.feickert@cern.ch>
Subject: [PATCH] Skip the runtime TLS probe of libnng when cross-compiling

configure runs a small program to check that the system libnng has working
TLS, and silently compiles the bundled NNG if the program fails. A program
built for the target platform cannot run when cross-compiling, which would
select the bundled NNG instead of the conda-forge nng, so trust the system
libnng when the build_platform and target_platform set by rattler-build
differ. The conda-forge nng is always built with Mbed TLS support.
---
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -236,7 +236,11 @@
     # A system libnng can pass the version and link checks yet have no TLS at
     # runtime: nng_tls_config_alloc() always exists, as an ENOTSUP stub if need
     # be. Probe by running it -- any failure selects the bundled build.
-    if echo "#include <nng/nng.h>
+    # The probe cannot run when cross-compiling, so then trust the system libnng.
+    if [ -n "$build_platform" ] && [ "$build_platform" != "$target_platform" ]; then
+      echo "Cross-compiling... skipping the runtime TLS probe"
+      echo "Found 'libnng' $NNG_SYS_CFLAGS"
+    elif echo "#include <nng/nng.h>
 #include <nng/supplemental/tls/tls.h>
 int main(void) {
     nng_tls_config *cfg;
